.TH FEISHU-GRAB 1 "October 9, 2026" "Feishu Grabber 1.3.0"
.SH NAME
feishu-grab \- export Feishu and Lark documents using daily Chrome
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B feishu-grab
.RI [ export ] " url ... " [ options ]
.br
.B feishu-grab current
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B feishu-grab doctor
.RI [ --json ] " [--timeout seconds]"
.br
.B feishu-grab report
.I export-report.json
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B feishu-grab completion
.I bash|zsh|fish
.br
.B feishu-grab help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B feishu-grab version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Exports HTTPS Feishu/Lark docx, document wiki, and docs links to local Markdown
with assets and integrity reports. Daily Chrome is the default browser mode
and uses macOS AppleScript. Authentication remains in Chrome.
.PP
Enable Chrome's View > Developer > Allow JavaScript from Apple Events setting.
If prompted, allow your terminal to control Google Chrome in macOS Automation
privacy settings. The program does not enable these permissions automatically.
Keep the intended signed-in Chrome profile's window open during export.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o ", " --out " directory"
Output directory. Defaults to ~/Downloads.
.TP
.B --list file
Read UTF-8 URLs, one per line. Ignore blank lines and lines starting with #.
.TP
.B --retry report
Retry documents that did not reach complete in a previous export report.
.TP
.B --current
Include the active document in daily Chrome.
Also available as the current command.
.TP
.B --browser chrome|isolated
Use daily Chrome (default) or the existing Chrome for Testing profile.
.TP
.BR -f ", " --format " md|pdf|html|capture"
Output format. Defaults to md. Daily Chrome supports Markdown only.
Other formats require --browser isolated.
.TP
.B --timeout seconds
Positive request timeout. Defaults to 180 seconds.
.TP
.B --render-fallback
Allow a rendered DOM or screenshot fallback in isolated mode.
The compatibility alias --allow-focus is also accepted.
.TP
.B --doctor
Compatibility alias for the doctor command.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage or command help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " -v ", " --version
Show the installed version.
.SH OUTPUT
Each run writes document files, downloaded assets, export-report.json,
index.html, and retry-urls.txt. Integrity verdicts are complete, degraded
(completeness unproven), or incomplete (known missing content or resources).
An output file alone does not prove a complete export.
.PP
The report command inspects these results without connecting to Chrome.
The --json option prints the original report. Doctor --json prints connection
state; successful connection does not prove authentication or document access.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every exported or reported document is complete; non-export commands succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure.
.TP
.B 2
At least one document is degraded or incomplete, without an operational failure.
.TP
.B 64
Invalid arguments or an invalid report schema.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
feishu-grab doctor
feishu-grab 'https://example.feishu.cn/wiki/TOKEN' --out ./exports
feishu-grab current --out ./exports
feishu-grab export --list urls.txt --out ./exports
feishu-grab report ./exports/export-report.json --json
feishu-grab help export
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Daily session reuse requires macOS and Google Chrome. CORS restrictions,
CSRF-protected read APIs, inaccessible resources, and unsupported blocks
may result in degraded or incomplete exports. Native documents and browser
profiles are not modified. Existing tabs are preserved; temporary export
tabs are closed after use unless navigated by the user.
